From 122fa16005408ef30e9c83557f8d1ab7b78e468f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:41:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 05/28] Eden (Doris): stop new CPU Async textures from flashing
 in

With ASTC decoding on CPU Async, Eden draws a new texture before its decode is done and only uploads
it at the end of a later frame, so new places flash as textures fill in. Doris waits for the decode
it just queued, from a budget of doris_texture_decode_wait_ms per frame (default 8 ms), and uploads
the result right away; if the budget runs out it falls back to Eden's end-of-frame upload.
Decoding also uses doris_texture_decode_threads background threads (default 2, Eden 1).
